      The title is what makes the plate below wearable. PawnGenerator sets the
      faction's ideoligion and the title before GenerateGearFor, and under a
      hierarchy ideoligion an untitled Obsidian may not wear RR_ArmorRestricted
      plate - so without this every knight came out in work clothes (0 of 10 in
      the rrtestmode=kinds run, review RV-03). Titles go to the generating faction
      when it has RR_ServiceTitle in its royalTitleTags, as the Society does.
    -->
    <titleRequired>RR_Title_Praetorian</titleRequired>
    <apparelTags Inherit="False">
      <!-- The trusted Obsidian: this kind IS the Praetorian case the armour rule describes. -->
      <li>RR_HeavyPlate</li>
      <!-- Clothing to wear under it; with only an armour tag the
           generator has nothing to buy but plate. -->
      <li>IndustrialBasic</li>
    </apparelTags>
    <weaponTags>
      <li>MedievalMeleeAdvanced</li>
      <li>UltratechMelee</li>
    </weaponTags>
    <skills>
